{
 "_comment": "lumora_outskirts_spawns.json - 3D spawn definitions for Lumora Outskirts zone. Positions are [x, y, z] world coords. Y=2 ensures spawn above terrain so mobs drop to ground via gravity. Layout matches the zone's hand-drawn area map (2026-09-14 balance pass): Sand Dunes starter area near the origin, Mausoleum/Graveyard/Crypts undead cluster to the southeast, Bandit Camps strung between the dunes and the Goblin Camps to the northwest, and a dedicated Spider Den to the southwest. | 2026-09-20: max_active is now PER ENTRY (each spawn point's own cap; before it was shared by every entry of the same mob type). Gate ring and the mausoleum/graveyard were thinned out, and small groups were added along the roads between the landmarks. 'density' multiplies every max_active (1.0 = as written). 'activation_range' (400 m) = a spawn point only makes mobs while a player is that close, so far parts of the zone cost nothing until someone gets there. | 'deep_dunes_south': two RARE Sunmaddened wanderer spawn points in the far south (level 4-6, tough; each drops a Ceramic Water-Token for the Release the Hollowed quest): a 2%/second chance while a player is within range and an 8 minute wait after each one dies. no_monster_zones: rectangles ({min:[x,z], max:[x,z]}) where monsters never spawn and never wander on their own (chasing a player in, and gate raids, still can).",
